WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.609
That's New York Democratic

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.679
Congressman Jamaal Bowman arguing

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.449
with Kentucky Republican Thomas

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.399
Massie over how to stop school

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.559
shootings like the one in Nashville

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.449
that left three students and

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.709
three adults dead.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.419
It's understandable that tempers

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.039
flare and voices rise in the

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.259
aftermath of such horrific events.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.539
When faced with such situations,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.369
the urge to do something, to do

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:32.649
anything is nearly impossible

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.669
to resist.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.529
But is Congressman Bowman right

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.359
that more guns lead to more

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.439
deaths?

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.969
The short answer is no.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.769
Over the past few decades, the

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.209
number of guns in America has

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.219
increased massively, so much so

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.869
that there are now more guns than

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.609
people in the United States.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.439
Yet federal crime statistics say

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.509
that firearm homicides dropped

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.119
about 40% between 1993

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.559
and 2018.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.539
For other crimes involving guns,

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.609
the decline was 71%.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.334
Violent crime did spike during COVID

00:01:02.335 --> 00:01:04.179
and while the most recent data is

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.009
incomplete, it's clear that

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:08.049
gun related violence remains far

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.999
below where it was 30 years

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.979
ago, despite more guns than

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.359
ever being out there.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.459
That's great news, especially

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.079
since reducing the number of guns in

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.029
circulation presents not just

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.949
immense pragmatic challenges,

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.139
but almost certainly insuperable

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.729
constitutional barriers.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.379
When it comes to schools, the

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.389
2020-2021 academic

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.039
year, the latest for which full data

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.319
is available, did see the highest

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.579
number of school shootings with

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.409
casualties this century.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:36.819
Thankfully, there are too few

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.409
violent deaths to generate

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.939
statistically significant

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.049
conclusions.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:42.909
But the long term trends show

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.369
no increase in homicides or suicides

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.229
among students, staff and

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:48.099
teachers.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.079
Overall, schools are becoming safer

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.489
and safer, with the government

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.349
finding that between 2009 and

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.479
2020, non-fatal crime

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.399
rates dropped for students ages 12

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.249
to 18, from 51

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.250
to 11 victimization

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.549
per 1000 students.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.139
What about Congressman Massey's

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:05.979
contention?

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.659
You know, there's never been a

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:10.448
shooting in a school that allows

00:02:10.449 --> 00:02:12.009
teachers to carry.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.779
He appears to be correct, though

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.249
contrary to his claim that there's

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.959
never been an accidental weapons

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.579
discharge by a teacher.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:20.589
A January 2023 RAND

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.239
Corporation study found that

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.859
teachers have indeed been involved

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.319
in accidental discharges of weapons.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.089
On the larger question of arming

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.099
teachers. RAND simply says

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.659
there isn't good enough data on

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.399
whether doing so would increase gun

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.349
violence or reduce it across

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.449
eight categories, such as stopping

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.859
mass shootings or preventing

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.849
suicides.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.469
What, then, is to be done?

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.269
Most schools are already gun free

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.249
zones or have strict controls

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.989
on who's allowed to carry while on

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:47.829
campus.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.289
Many have armed officers on campus,

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.299
despite no evidence that such

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.189
a presence deters violence.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.689
Recent school shootings, like the

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.849
one last year involving Texas,

00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.619
where law enforcement officials not

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.209
only did nothing to prevent an

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.099
active shooter, but restrained

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.719
parents trying to rescue their

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.609
children. Underscore that police

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.259
need better and more effective

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.039
training.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.349
The 2018 school shooting at Marjory

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:12.909
Stoneman Douglas High School in

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.919
Florida highlighted how many red

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.839
flags, school staff, police

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.609
and social workers had ignored.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.559
It's deeply unsatisfying to

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.569
simply say that the people

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:24.429
in charge of school safety need to

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.629
do better.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.819
But it might be the best option,

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.319
especially if the rush to do

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.059
something means trying something

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.279
that we already know is impossible,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.830
ineffective, or both.

